  "result": "I fixed the bug. `IntRange(..., clamp=True)` with an open bound (`min_open` or `max_open`) returned a value outside the allowed range. `tests/test_types.py` passes, including the new cases; I didn't run the full suite.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py` moved away from an open bound instead of into the range. It computed `bound - dir`, where it should compute `bound + dir`. For example, `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-1` returned `-1` instead of `1`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- The fix is that one-line change in `src/click/types.py`.\n- I added two regression cases to `test_range` in `tests/test_types.py`: `min_open` with `-1` now gives `1`, and `max_open` with `9` now gives `4`.\n- I added an entry to `CHANGES.md` under a new \"Version 8.5.1 / Unreleased\" heading. The top section was 8.5.0, which is already released, so I made a new one. Rename it if you version differently.\n\nI didn't touch `docs/`, because this is a bug fix and no documented behaviour changes.",
